<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime, not sandboxed: no exceptions are needed.
  - No com.apple.security.cs.* exceptions: the app loads no unsigned code and needs no JIT
    (WebKit's JIT runs in Apple's own WebContent process).
  - No App Sandbox (com.apple.security.app-sandbox): Developer ID distribution does not require it,
    and turning it on would move the app's data into a container (existing queue, screenshots and
    prefs would no longer be found) and needs a review of the activity collector under the sandbox.
    com.apple.security.network.client only applies to sandboxed apps, so it is not listed.
  - Screen Recording (ScreenCaptureKit) and Keychain need no entitlement; Screen Recording is a
    TCC permission the employee grants in System Settings.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
